 "notes": "Hidden-photon kinetic mixing limit from the CERN microwave light-shining-through-wall run of March 2012 (11.5 h at f_sys = 2.9565 GHz, P_det = -211 dBm). Curve traced from the vector paths of Fig. 2 (e-print file exclusion.pdf, the cyan 'Microwave LSW March 2012 CERN' region), calibrated against the axis tick marks; the extracted minimum chi = 7.7e-9 at m = 1.08e-5 eV matches the annotation chi = 7.6e-9 at m = 1.1e-5 eV/c^2. The boundary follows chi ~ m^-2 below the resonance and rises steeply at the photon-energy cutoff m = h*f_sys = 1.22e-5 eV (last point). Laboratory LSW limit: no dark-matter density assumption, so no rescaling. The paper does not state an explicit confidence level (limit set by the maximum noise peak in the search window); 0.95 entered as the conventional value.",
